er/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439678} :answer-field/id #uuid "bcd10ed6-e678-5883-b02e-6ab8e9a29d8b" :answer-field/key "$p(x) → ∞$ as $x → ∞$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440196}] :question/id #uuid "6659c5a9-8cd4-5728-b7f7-08c5ba5aeadd" :question/math-academy-id "q-38768" :question/problem "![](images/4b/4b91ee95f42770036434909f2bb62102120f85f464e548a0142a603164a41b32.png)\n\nThe graph of a polynomial $p(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The graph crosses at x=0 (odd multiplicity) and touches/turns at x=-1 and x=2 (even multiplicities). Its right-hand tail rises, giving p(x) tending to positive infinity."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129771 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129113 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5d1d859-0b86-5507-a7bf-3d805a85adf3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Augmented Matrices in Row Echelon Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b6ac301d-037b-5334-b6d2-fec88197d154" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459951} {:answer/id #uuid "5d1e6f74-c495-5ab5-805c-d983bca1e55c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459952}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d1e6f74-c495-5ab5-805c-d983bca1e55c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459952} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d0e98e1-9e1f-510d-9dad-15a86b32835a" :answer-field/key "$A=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 3 & -7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 5\\end{array}\\right]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460842} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b9aa059-0eae-5a76-81c6-21892541d8ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459953} {:answer/id #uuid "0816847a-d539-509b-8356-6a24a780f633" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459954}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0816847a-d539-509b-8356-6a24a780f633" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459954} :answer-field/id #uuid "5488b353-c1b4-5e30-83ca-a801084429aa" :answer-field/key "$B=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}3 & 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460843} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fd314e1a-8262-5acc-90db-8b8b4a9f82f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459955} {:answer/id #uuid "69a17d39-0448-5a32-8559-ff5820bddc16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459956}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd314e1a-8262-5acc-90db-8b8b4a9f82f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459955} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb9e86fc-fb03-5653-aa77-b599aca20dc9" :answer-field/key "$C=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 & 2\\end{array}\\right]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460844}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "658776f4-d49a-5e5d-a10c-50a3db34ad1c" :question/math-academy-id "q-42006" :question/problem "Which of the following augmented matrices are in row echelon form?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the bottom of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column to the right of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 3 & -7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 5\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}3 & 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is not in row echelon form since ${c}_{22}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nC=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 & 2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $B$ are in row echelon form."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129773 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129114 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d390841-351e-54f5-ad19-90b6ebae5799" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Matrices in Row Echelon Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "836635cc-25da-5e83-aec4-49f375758900" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459957} {:answer/id #uuid "54eea2b5-b542-5880-be19-6f511782168a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459958}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "836635cc-25da-5e83-aec4-49f375758900" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459957} :answer-field/id #uuid "04197247-7f0f-56bf-a021-b95053e007e5" :answer-field/key "$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460845} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29bb0349-8228-5739-b584-2b4184c57825" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459959} {:answer/id #uuid "213dd0db-1f16-57b8-a75a-94405f576b31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459960}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "213dd0db-1f16-57b8-a75a-94405f576b31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459960} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1992ae7-8a06-5253-8bae-a159ecd12de1" :answer-field/key "$B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 & 6 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460846} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93932082-4e2a-5d11-9338-3badee54015f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459961} {:answer/id #uuid "3337fae3-8c3b-5ced-a2fe-a0e0b650426e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459962}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3337fae3-8c3b-5ced-a2fe-a0e0b650426e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459962} :answer-field/id #uuid "da567c2d-7ca3-5ce0-9d1f-676b0894d8d6" :answer-field/key "$C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 5 & 8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460847}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "181e77e0-d595-5539-baef-b4986d4c678b" :question/math-academy-id "q-42024" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are in row echelon form?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since the second row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 & 6 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 5 & 8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $B$ and $C$ are in row echelon form."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129836 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129086 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9110c50a-62db-5447-b4d0-60819c80eb31" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Properties Related to Point Discontinuities Given a Function Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7bb3ef39-24f4-53fd-ad23-80e8401afa50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460155} {:answer/id #uuid "3ce78283-ea7a-5168-8a04-a0032f00df30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460156}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ce78283-ea7a-5168-8a04-a0032f00df30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460156} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5b52c2d-ba98-5b84-9117-102d22385b70" :answer-field/key "${lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}g(x)={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}g(x)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460944} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66729ae8-8043-572c-bc7d-a1c624ce8fdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460157} {:answer/id #uuid "9d688561-b6b3-5263-b56a-63b6c54dbfd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460158}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d688561-b6b3-5263-b56a-63b6c54dbfd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460158} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7cfdd66-3b1c-5a02-8cb9-f68ca2e8601d" :answer-field/key "${lim}_{x\\to 1}g(x)=g(1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460945} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "606315b7-0138-573f-8c5f-15212b7196f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460159} {:answer/id #uuid "ebe69130-7731-5cc0-9c45-c94262ef9b41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460160}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "606315b7-0138-573f-8c5f-15212b7196f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460159} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e9cb025-b523-5afd-9e2b-488c18701756" :answer-field/key "$g(x)$ has a removable discontinuity at $x=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460946}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "de45d0f1-1f5a-51b7-a854-73bfcba5bbdc" :question/math-academy-id "q-71181" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(x) & ={\\begin{aligned}5x-5, & x<1 \\\\ 0, & x=1 \\\\ {x}^{3}-1, & x>1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's check our continuity conditions:\n\n- $g(1)=0$ exists $\\,✓$\n\n- The left and right-sided limits are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{-}}g(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{-}}(5x-5)=5(1)-5=0, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{+}}g(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{+}}({x}^{3}-1)={1}^{3}-1=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the left and right-sided limits are equal, we conclude that statement ${lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}g(x)={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}g(x)$ is true and\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 1}g(x)=0.\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\n- The value of the limit is ${lim}_{x\\to 1}g(x)=0,$ and the value of the function is $g(1)=0.$ So, statement ${lim}_{x\\to 1}g(x)=g(1)$ is true and\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 1}g(x)=g(1)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nSo, the function is continuous at $x=0,$ and statement “$g(x)$ has a removable discontinuity at $x=1$” is false.\n\nIn conclusion, only statements ${lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}g(x)={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}g(x)$ and ${lim}_{x\\to 1}g(x)=g(1)$ are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129841 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129169 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7948909f-8dcb-5cc0-a00f-f505a41e4004" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a Region as Type I, Type II, Both, or Neither"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd96f985-646a-5351-b253-f0f95e8d6cc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460167} {:answer/id #uuid "fec5ba87-c419-560c-b2ba-bfc88d02a82e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460168}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fec5ba87-c419-560c-b2ba-bfc88d02a82e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460168} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ebca1f5-c590-5037-9705-2d669297c270" :answer-field/key "It is a type I region" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460950} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a3ff502-9a19-5d3d-b530-9a9bf3e410d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460169} {:answer/id #uuid "45de598b-3b91-5235-928b-a27046c1368a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460170}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "45de598b-3b91-5235-928b-a27046c1368a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460170} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4a62c74-c650-5a78-92c1-6052f0293257" :answer-field/key "It is a type II region" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460951} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4406943e-20a0-5c47-9f3b-12422d2366ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460171} {:answer/id #uuid "a14b7932-a9aa-55ab-87a0-b0dcf56024dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460172}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4406943e-20a0-5c47-9f3b-12422d2366ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460171} :answer-field/id #uuid "a353e8b3-884f-5bc4-bb00-c6d7f9c98968" :answer-field/key "It's neither a type I nor a type II region" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460952}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b84b6274-fa65-5873-af84-3d0475556d93" :question/math-academy-id "q-71892" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region bounded between the parabola $y=1-{x}^{2}$ and the line $y=-3?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that\n\n$$\ny=1-{x}^{2}\\,⟹\\,x=\\pm \\sqrt{1-y}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](images/72/726ad8599b89029d3dba8e79ca947af99c17bd8712e551e49fc33d3e597a5cb7.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- Any vertical line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,-3\\le y\\le 1-{x}^{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type I region.\n\n- Any horizontal line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-3\\le y\\le 1,\\,-\\sqrt{1-y}\\le x\\le \\sqrt{1-y}\\}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type II region.\n\nTherefore, only statements “It is a type I region” and “It is a type II region” are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129842 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129169 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7948909f-8dcb-5cc0-a00f-f505a41e4004" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a Region as Type I, Type II, Both, or Neither"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55a6ee0a-d96f-565a-b86b-753fef10bcb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460173} {:answer/id #uuid "c5fa2d01-0363-5414-aee0-15a329ab0bd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460174}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "55a6ee0a-d96f-565a-b86b-753fef10bcb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460173} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ad56762-b330-5bb1-8ba0-9869f5af2ead" :answer-field/key "It is a type I region" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460953} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3f634cf-ea4c-5e68-b5da-4eef1c1c56af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460175} {:answer/id #uuid "49f35556-5b7c-515b-9a7a-4189930ec2c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460176}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3f634cf-ea4c-5e68-b5da-4eef1c1c56af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460175} :answer-field/id #uuid "409900db-4264-516b-b459-9b27a44721c2" :answer-field/key "It is a type II region" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460954} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34ae5851-54cb-53e1-a0fe-3cb10c69a3f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460177} {:answer/id #uuid "58d69edb-8d2a-5ce7-bef1-d0329b4c1d8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460178}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58d69edb-8d2a-5ce7-bef1-d0329b4c1d8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460178} :answer-field/id #uuid "f764f310-ac1b-5163-8ef9-b2f704f3384e" :answer-field/key "It's neither a type I nor a type II region" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460955}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7805c1fc-f8dc-58be-9c44-d22a8226c755" :question/math-academy-id "q-71895" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region bounded between the circles ${x}^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=1$ and ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](images/24/24cbd9a0e01023dca6a289838d94efe3c7b67abe5b7a1f275f6945f280e65d64.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- The vertical line $x=0.75$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type I region.\n\n![](images/6c/6c51abe5c21571a9c5596fce4e3b8ace210eacfab125016e6b9a3b2a7bc2e056.png)\n\n- The horizontal line $y=1$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type II region.\n\n![](images/f9/f9fed5856eda128d84debec320bc38a35eaa2bf5184b1f81cb1194b02f8a306a.png)\n\nTherefore, only statement “It's neither a type I nor a type II region” is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129843 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129166 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8f012d0-444a-5035-8a72-a053de312d63" :knowledge-point/title "Changing the Order of Integration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91568609-53f1-5507-b633-85ad296ed987" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477401} {:answer/id #uuid "abfa74e5-1a47-59ee-a292-457310b3664b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477402}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91568609-53f1-5507-b633-85ad296ed987" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477401} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3f6473f-924a-5e41-985c-db027a5ee1a0" :answer-field/key "${∬}_{D}y\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{3}y\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477670} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "012a6d65-60d0-51a7-925b-0e49757fe3be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477403} {:answer/id #uuid "da1badff-0793-561c-8adb-2219ff40b36f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477404}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da1badff-0793-561c-8adb-2219ff40b36f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477404} :answer-field/id #uuid "271ed790-21f1-5ed8-b43c-01e1c50b54ec" :answer-field/key "${∬}_{D}y\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{3}y\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477671} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1f80a26-5433-5863-82c5-245dff2f8e6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477405} {:answer/id #uuid "ad596bf8-98cc-5eea-a484-dd4ec22f3bdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477406}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a1f80a26-5433-5863-82c5-245dff2f8e6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477405} :answer-field/id #uuid "81f64dcb-9d5d-5899-8167-8ee4eef5397f" :answer-field/key "${∬}_{D}y\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477672}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fd6a034f-87ae-5507-9abe-98641b443d7e" :question/math-academy-id "q-71930" :question/problem "Which of the following equalities are true given that\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,1\\le y\\le 3\\}.$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We notice that:\n\n- the limits for the variable $x$ are from $0$ to $1$, and\n\n- the limits for the variable $y$ are from $1$ to $3.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}y\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the region of integration is rectangular, we can simply swap the order of integration. This gives\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}y\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{1}^{3}y\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is ${∬}_{D}y\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{3}y\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134055 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133870 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2bcfcb6-8f8b-5aa9-8346-05db880fa5bb" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Set of Polynomials is Orthogonal With Respect to a Given Inner Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "503d7110-6cc5-5cf2-87e2-1045c8a36886" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459341} {:answer/id #uuid "d57ce771-3028-5baa-b0f2-f4de7d3617d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459342}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d57ce771-3028-5baa-b0f2-f4de7d3617d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459342} :answer-field/id #uuid "1af3661f-6783-5478-b5e6-eede91cb4aa6" :answer-field/key "${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460537} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9564e0ca-db68-5b0e-bdf8-c5593c07408e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459343} {:answer/id #uuid "fdd76439-cdc4-56b2-bd84-3cb9d3bce0cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459344}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fdd76439-cdc4-56b2-bd84-3cb9d3bce0cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459344} :answer-field/id #uuid "80d76efe-3861-569a-b729-ec393ecd874e" :answer-field/key "${p}_{1}(t)⊥̸{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460538} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60137c2c-ff15-5a99-a0a7-4cfa1f1442f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459345} {:answer/id #uuid "cff078f1-3b0f-5053-b2a0-745dbd7d061e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459346}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60137c2c-ff15-5a99-a0a7-4cfa1f1442f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459345} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec498012-39b0-5787-b344-2b214924c219" :answer-field/key "$S=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460539}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "97d43a34-aeb6-5e6a-8281-47dcdcd73020" :question/math-academy-id "q-100128" :question/problem "Consider the following set of polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=2t,\\,{p}_{2}(t)=t+1,\\,{p}_{3}(t)=2t+1.\n$$\n\nGiven that the inner product in the vector space ${R}_{1}[t]$ of polynomials of degree at most $1$ in the variable $t$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=p(0)q(0)+p(-1)q(-1),\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a set of vectors in an inner product space is orthogonal if all vectors in the set are mutually orthogonal with respect to the given inner product. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” is true. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)⟩ & =⟨2t,t+1⟩ \\\\  & =(2t){|}_{0}\\cdot (t+1){|}_{0}+(2t){|}_{-1}\\cdot (t+1){|}_{-1} \\\\  & =2(0)\\cdot (0+1)+2(-1)\\cdot ((-1)+1) \\\\  & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement “${p}_{1}(t)⊥̸{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” is true since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{3}(t)⟩ & =⟨2t,2t+1⟩ \\\\  & =(2t){|}_{0}\\cdot (2t+1){|}_{0}+(2t){|}_{-1}\\cdot (2t+1){|}_{-1} \\\\  & =2(0)\\cdot (2(0)+1)+2(-1)\\cdot (2(-1)+1) \\\\  & =2\\ne 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${p}_{1}(t)⊥̸{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement “$S=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product” is false. Since ${p}_{1}(t)⊥̸{p}_{3}(t),$ the set $S$ is *not* orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product”; “${p}_{1}(t)⊥̸{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134061 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133880 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f47e201-105a-579a-8cde-fcb6bf8cfa2a" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting Divergence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e37611b-b4ca-5379-847c-3a7765d404fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439393} {:answer/id #uuid "765faeb0-ed48-53f3-b1eb-c5a6f7e2135b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439394}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e37611b-b4ca-5379-847c-3a7765d404fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439393} :answer-field/id #uuid "b65cb51f-ba83-56b7-9dc2-4a765d918943" :answer-field/key "$\\text{div}\\,F=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440054} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "394b0c92-413b-5182-bf86-908b31bea2d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439395} {:answer/id #uuid "a5a2bf22-912d-55ed-9446-5abda1fe8202" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439396}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "394b0c92-413b-5182-bf86-908b31bea2d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439395} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7014164-d3a8-54e0-b2b2-69b7a546b3ee" :answer-field/key "$\\text{div}\\,F>0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440055} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d66ca4c-dc58-584c-976f-6c65dcb0374b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439397} {:answer/id #uuid "2b1a3581-91b7-51be-a39a-394d06c35627" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439398}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b1a3581-91b7-51be-a39a-394d06c35627" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439398} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c3322fa-b621-5555-b3ed-1f86ce1470ea" :answer-field/key "$\\text{div}\\,F<0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440056} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c747585-3d2c-5bc7-bfaa-a6485611b22f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439399} {:answer/id #uuid "36fe6723-4807-59df-ae7e-c3f3add34f97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439400}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c747585-3d2c-5bc7-bfaa-a6485611b22f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439399} :answer-field/id #uuid "56a24dae-9028-5f6f-bfb1-b8f7462e6a64" :answer-field/key "$F$ is solenoidal" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440057}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d82a128a-970f-55e8-b4ad-4c3c16a14935" :question/math-academy-id "q-105075" :question/problem "![](images/34/3411e11060b06a11c82ad677f50731faa31c6bc2e83ccb0d0d10931cf3d76592.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true everywhere in the domain of $F?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{div}\\,F=∇\\cdot F$ denotes the divergence of the vector field $F.$\n\nIntuitively, the divergence of $F$ at a point $P$ measures how much $F$ acts like a source or a sink at $P:$\n\n- If $∇\\cdot F>0$ at $P,$ then $F$ acts like a source at $P.$\n\n- If $∇\\cdot F<0$ at $P,$ then $F$ acts like a sink at $P.$\n\n- If $∇\\cdot F=0$ at $P,$ then $F$ acts like neither a source nor a sink at $P.$\n\n![](images/6c/6c747149618d4c5ef35e727af15cd001365bd9c2d5e064689baf24c6ee23cff9.png)\n\nIf $∇\\cdot F=0$ everywhere in the domain of $F,$ we say that $F$ is solenoidal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement $\\text{div}\\,F<0$ is true, whereas statements $\\text{div}\\,F=0$ and $\\text{div}\\,F>0$ are false. Notice that the lengths of the vectors decrease as we move in the $y$-direction. Therefore, the vector field $F$ acts like a sink at every point.\n\n- Statement “$F$ is solenoidal” is false. Since $∇\\cdot F\\ne 0,$ the vector field $F$ is not solenoidal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{div}\\,F<0$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134062 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133881 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d42243ea-58fc-53f6-a0b6-f995bf1d697c" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Curl of a Vector Field"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64adfa84-016b-5b75-bfaa-1a8a86ec6cff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437398} {:answer/id #uuid "74db0023-87ca-59a4-a5bd-f3ec8e8116b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437399}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74db0023-87ca-59a4-a5bd-f3ec8e8116b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437399} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8d82e25-5382-533b-84b7-01e9f7a1d6d9" :answer-field/key "$\\text{curl}\\,F=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438728} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8567ee77-d4f1-5260-9f23-476c33065db6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437400} {:answer/id #uuid "a70669e9-818c-5056-9e48-6b53420d42e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437401}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8567ee77-d4f1-5260-9f23-476c33065db6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437400} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4ff09e7-c874-5a69-a376-7cc151c1b301" :answer-field/key "$\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438729} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bdbd1a0c-db83-58a6-82a4-5124aff61305" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437402} {:answer/id #uuid "66a86276-9dec-5106-ae18-146b9a8a0341" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437403}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "66a86276-9dec-5106-ae18-146b9a8a0341" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437403} :answer-field/id #uuid "76eb44c2-5da3-5456-a3ae-c27f914fb121" :answer-field/key "$F$ is irrotational" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438730} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c36d028-9a19-523f-8a50-c043c1583d10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437404} {:answer/id #uuid "f9c4fd28-7364-51cd-9702-c77f2ad2fba7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437405}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c36d028-9a19-523f-8a50-c043c1583d10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437404} :answer-field/id #uuid "455d8cf9-d20d-599d-bbf0-180199060744" :answer-field/key "$\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the negative $z$-direction." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438731}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7a72f589-a1bb-57d0-9bf2-23704868e98f" :question/math-academy-id "q-105092" :question/problem "![](images/38/38a7ae83a66a2c1ff6a012b9405c6621b0c0a162018065549e75a1d08bc04d44.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y,z),$ shown above. Given that $F(x,y,z)$ is independent of $z,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{curl}\\,F$ denotes the curl of the vector field $F.$\n\nTo understand intuitively whether a vector field has curl at a point $P$, imagine that our vector field $F$ represents the velocity field of a stream of flowing water. We place a paddlewheel at $P$ with the axis of rotation pointing in the $z$-direction, and we note whether the paddlewheel rotates or not.\n\n- If the paddlewheel does not rotate due to the action of the water, then the velocity field has zero curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F=0.$\n\n- If the paddlewheel is forced to rotate due to the action of the water, then the vector field has curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n![](images/59/594106633e422d24b9fea113d24fb6367fdef5ac52724931860e4163e33ce992.png)\n\nMoreover, if $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$ everywhere in ${R}^{3}$, we say that $F$ is irrotational.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$ is true, whereas statement $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$ is false. If a paddlewheel were placed at any point $P$ in the manner described above, it would not rotate. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F=0.$\n\n- Statements “$F$ is irrotational” is true. Since $\\text{curl}\\,F=0,$ the vector field $F$ is irrotational.\n\n- Statement “$\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the negative $z$-direction” is false. Since $\\text{curl}\\,F=0,$ it points in neither the positive nor the negative $z$-direction.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$; “$F$ is irrotational” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134063 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133881 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d42243ea-58fc-53f6-a0b6-f995bf1d697c" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Curl of a Vector Field"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba17fd4c-8a29-5e53-98c2-ac71e936d451" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439401} {:answer/id #uuid "829d51be-bbb4-5302-8892-638706b87aa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439402}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ba17fd4c-8a29-5e53-98c2-ac71e936d451" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439401} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0a7c437-986c-533d-b681-b536d