er/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459534}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f536b65-945c-5069-ade1-ce17175a0b7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459533} :answer-field/id #uuid "2bbf7638-1805-5c9a-962c-88753c4aaa5e" :answer-field/key "None of the children spend less than $2$ hours playing outdoors." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460633}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1109475d-9e0b-5521-b99e-3e1bd3fbb649" :question/math-academy-id "q-133622" :question/problem "![](images/e4/e4b568fe2226154be401a2332c718f143954d98fdbd8a0c679fdb99fcdd47d14.png)\n\nSarah interviewed some parents, asking them how much time their children spend playing outdoors per day. The information she received is summarized in the scatter plot above. \n\nGiven that none of the points overlap, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our scatter plot.\n\n- Statement “There is only one child who spends $3.5$ hours playing outdoors” is true. The scatter plot has only one dot whose vertical coordinate equals $3.5,$ namely, $(5,3.5).$ This means that only one child spends $3.5$ hours playing outdoors.\n\n![](images/01/0103370189c7156f9677ca576e2480bc99314cd312702fca3ea3e50cb4f7287a.png)\n\n- Statement “There is only one child aged $6$ among those surveyed” is false. The scatter plot has two dots whose horizontal coordinate equals $6,$ namely, $(6,2)$ and $(6,2.5).$ This means that there were two children of age $6$ among those surveyed.\n\n![](images/0a/0a8ca9628b48e643e1aa9e9f0216148881db237c2d29054b29f4377ad182503d.png)\n\n- Statement “None of the children spend less than $2$ hours playing outdoors” is false. From the scatter plot, two children spend less than $2$ hours playing outdoors. Those children are represented by the two dots below the horizontal line.\n\n![](images/4d/4d9709c131045f2e440204f79ad3fd8ff22707312b0e99138da558393e8b7f6d.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “There is only one child who spends $3.5$ hours playing outdoors” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152419 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152234 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "35453324-c2ff-5be4-86aa-70b3085154dc" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting Information From a Scatter Plot"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67c58a8f-8248-5a1e-bc1a-ca754ff1bf9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459535} {:answer/id #uuid "a165f429-0191-5e83-9162-d845ecf57294" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459536}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67c58a8f-8248-5a1e-bc1a-ca754ff1bf9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459535} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ed19dd8-2331-58ee-8e63-5060c63df0a4" :answer-field/key "Only one player has a shoe size of $9\\frac{1}{2}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460634} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27072f06-b04e-5738-828a-97b69f152668" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459537} {:answer/id #uuid "27d7d283-6013-5e3b-a892-3787a588a476" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459538}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27d7d283-6013-5e3b-a892-3787a588a476" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459538} :answer-field/id #uuid "79cb274f-9e25-59dc-936b-c4b047a0d929" :answer-field/key "Only one player is $195\\,\\text{cm}$ tall." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460635} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d9232092-31bd-57de-b974-cc58445adee5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459539} {:answer/id #uuid "041282ea-d595-54e1-9a5e-7b57ffe6c62c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459540}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9232092-31bd-57de-b974-cc58445adee5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459539} :answer-field/id #uuid "71a0be3f-582c-5cfd-9a1e-7daefb5e53f6" :answer-field/key "There are exactly two players taller than $185\\,\\text{cm}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460636}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "35f73958-c27b-5887-a2cc-b747d3896473" :question/math-academy-id "q-134133" :question/problem "![](images/b2/b25aa3b36011df9f9a97ca55fce75b2bf53b6b35282d8d5896e348464d4bdd30.png)\n\nMr. Clark recorded the height and shoe size of the players on the basketball team he coaches. The information he collected is summarized in the scatter plot above. \n\nGiven that none of the points overlap, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our scatter plot.\n\n- Statement “Only one player has a shoe size of $9\\frac{1}{2}.$” is false. The scatter plot has two dots whose vertical coordinate equals $9.5,$ namely, $(180,9.5)$ and $(195,9.5).$ This means that two players have a shoe size of  $9\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\n![](images/c2/c2058bf02025ff359b509db01022c5d2e956d67243094a33692b90d6f1c2eac8.png)\n\n \n\n- Statement “Only one player is $195\\,\\text{cm}$ tall” is true. The scatter plot has only one dot whose horizontal coordinate equals $195,$ namely, $(195,\\,9.5).$ This means that only one of the players has a height of $195\\,\\text{cm}.$\n\n![](images/b8/b8b4364dc5de11eed12840bc644b1392b36160adfdf739b96f282c2367d999fa.png)\n\n \n\n- Statement “There are exactly two players taller than $185\\,\\text{cm}.$” is false. According to the scatter diagram, three players have a height greater than  $185\\,\\text{cm},$ represented by the three dots to the right of the vertical line.\n\n![](images/aa/aaf6d496c56c3cdc5a47e1c09e7640d7a3caa05446a75b705c042a56c116cb98.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “Only one player is $195\\,\\text{cm}$ tall” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152435 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152081 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "114dedd9-ed3d-5d25-8616-030ea4bd84c9" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Involving Universal Quantifiers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21a1c490-317c-56af-aaca-8fe315e90d62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477185} {:answer/id #uuid "2518607a-8c2b-501d-8b13-9bf03d137d52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477186}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21a1c490-317c-56af-aaca-8fe315e90d62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477185} :answer-field/id #uuid "66c8d549-0e3a-576e-9c86-87535a5a9206" :answer-field/key "The truth set of $P(x)$ is $∅.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477562} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9796ece8-af66-5847-805c-91b18125e41c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477187} {:answer/id #uuid "4acb42d3-5f2b-5454-9ed8-31f6677e044b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477188}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4acb42d3-5f2b-5454-9ed8-31f6677e044b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477188} :answer-field/id #uuid "97b4e633-15d1-5177-9e2a-14276d22daa2" :answer-field/key "The truth set of $P(x)$ is $Z.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477563} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d079178a-6333-5a2a-9306-54c4175ac559" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477189} {:answer/id #uuid "48f20c90-f605-576f-9a0f-a28369d8d620" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477190}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48f20c90-f605-576f-9a0f-a28369d8d620" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477190} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b2831df-ecb4-57a2-a3ae-580a566a6931" :answer-field/key "$∀x\\in Z,\\,P(x).$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477564}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "04aa90b0-83c7-56f5-b7d0-c861a0b74dfa" :question/math-academy-id "q-171841" :question/problem "$\\,$ $P(x):$ $x-1<x.$\n\nGiven that the above predicate is defined over the universal set $Z,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The *universal quantification* of a predicate $P(x),$ defined over the universal set $U,$ transforms this predicate into a statement that we write as\n\n$$\n∀x\\in U,\\,P(x).\n$$\n\nThis statement is true if the predicate $P(x)$ is true on the entire universal set $U,$ i.e. if the truth set ${T}_{P}$ of the predicate coincides with the universal set $U:$\n\n$$\n{T}_{P}=U\n$$\n\nFirst, we solve the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-1 & <x \\\\ -1 & <0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the final condition is true for all $x\\in Z,$ we have that the truth set of our predicate is ${T}_{P}=Z.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement “The truth set of $P(x)$ is $∅.$” is false. The truth set is *not* empty.\n\n- Statement “The truth set of $P(x)$ is $Z.$” is true. Indeed, ${T}_{P}=Z.$\n\n- Statement $∀x\\in Z,\\,P(x).$ is true. Since ${T}_{P}$ coincides with the universal set, the statement $∀x\\in Z,\\,P(x)$ is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The truth set of $P(x)$ is $Z.$”; $∀x\\in Z,\\,P(x).$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152449 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152089 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6927f03c-aa7a-56ac-8cd0-c036a11aadc9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Truth Value of a Statement Involving Nested Quantifiers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba39854b-085d-534c-a818-4d8f97105187" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477191} {:answer/id #uuid "80569c26-276c-5761-871b-a72386f51886" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477192}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "80569c26-276c-5761-871b-a72386f51886" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477192} :answer-field/id #uuid "a06b620f-a29c-5355-a2fc-11acd7d59931" :answer-field/key "$∀\\,n\\in N,\\,1\\le n.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477565} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19ed1674-c09d-5d5c-80db-6504cdcd672e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477193} {:answer/id #uuid "e1c91bd6-f8a7-5c6d-ba8c-302b60bea216" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477194}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19ed1674-c09d-5d5c-80db-6504cdcd672e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477193} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e421bf7-2527-5421-8dd2-b19e1aa6b277" :answer-field/key "The truth set of the predicate $(\\,∀\\,n\\in N,\\,m\\le n\\,)$ is $N.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477566} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7eaca7f5-b237-5b59-a6ce-9748f957704d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477195} {:answer/id #uuid "2c76716d-5fd3-5bae-b01d-4b004579db6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477196}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7eaca7f5-b237-5b59-a6ce-9748f957704d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477195} :answer-field/id #uuid "923ec8a3-2737-59b3-b386-48b9611a4c3d" :answer-field/key "$∀\\,m,n\\in N,\\,m\\le n.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477567}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a6099760-d85e-5730-93dd-a4f12f20c95b" :question/math-academy-id "q-171904" :question/problem "Let $m\\in N$ and $n\\in N.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the statement \n\n$$\n∀\\,m,n\\in N,\\,m\\le n\n$$\n\nfrom option $∀\\,m,n\\in N,\\,m\\le n.$ reads as follows:\n\n$\\,$ For all natural $m$ and $n,$ we have $m\\le n.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement $∀\\,n\\in N,\\,1\\le n.$ is true, since $1\\le n$ for all natural numbers $n.$\n\n- Statement “The truth set of the predicate $(\\,∀\\,n\\in N,\\,m\\le n\\,)$ is $N.$” is false. For the predicate\n\n$$\nP(m):\\,∀\\,n\\in N,\\,m\\le n\n$$\n\nwe note that $P(m)$ is true for some $m\\in N$ and false for others. For example, \n\n$$\nP(1):\\,∀\\,n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\n$$\n\nis true. However, \n\n$$\nP(2):\\,∀\\,n\\in N,\\,2\\le n\n$$\n\nis false, since $2≰1.$\n\n- Statement $∀\\,m,n\\in N,\\,m\\le n.$ is false. The sentence \n\n$$\n(\\,∀\\,m,n\\in N,\\,m\\le n\\,)\n$$\n\n \ncan be written as\n\n$$\n∀m\\in N\\,(\\,\\underbrace{∀n\\in N,\\,m\\le n}_{P(m)}\\,)\n$$\n\nwhich is true whenever the inner predicate $P(m)$ is true over the universal set $N.$ But, according to statement “The truth set of the predicate $(\\,∀\\,n\\in N,\\,m\\le n\\,)$ is $N.$”, this is not the case.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $∀\\,n\\in N,\\,1\\le n.$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152453 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152077 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0bc3ecd-2da1-5951-abba-95da02dee826" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Necessary Conditions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fea0ec28-488a-5ed5-b23a-ee6a7c3b6152" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459629} {:answer/id #uuid "4ee31146-f63c-561c-9fe7-0190988d5191" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459630}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fea0ec28-488a-5ed5-b23a-ee6a7c3b6152" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459629} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a06e7ee-beff-537c-a848-af5ba595ae03" :answer-field/key "$x=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460681} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e80f37a5-ace9-5a66-9242-1b1a70a7a1d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459631} {:answer/id #uuid "c718208c-45b4-518a-b74d-4db5340e01c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459632}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e80f37a5-ace9-5a66-9242-1b1a70a7a1d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459631} :answer-field/id #uuid "5329ad17-fa05-5f55-a20c-b80b5f880455" :answer-field/key "$x<0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460682} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "390547a5-6535-52a6-90d4-0ab8f3425b5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459633} {:answer/id #uuid "b4e5daac-3bca-5c19-a1a9-7a49a6752cf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459634}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4e5daac-3bca-5c19-a1a9-7a49a6752cf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459634} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4747150-8f2b-5a96-b68d-c5bd579b15b1" :answer-field/key "$|x|<5$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460683}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3aa2864d-150b-53f6-8540-2485ff225138" :question/math-academy-id "q-172296" :question/problem "$\\,$ ${x}^{2}+2x-3=0$\n\nWhich of the following conditions are necessary for the above to be true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ being true *guarantees* that $N$ must also be true. Therefore, $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- For $S$ to be true, it is *necessary* that $N$ is true. Therefore, $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$ However, note that $N$ being true does *not* guarantee that $S$ is true.\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nIn our case, we need to find the conditions that are *necessary* from the given one:\n\n$$\n({x}^{2}+2x-3=0)\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}\n$$\n\nNote that the solution to the given equation is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+2x-3 & =0 \\\\ (x+3)(x-1) & =0 \\\\ x & =-3,1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given conditions.\n\n- Condition $x=1$ is *not* a necessary condition:\n\n$$\n({x}^{2}+2x-3=0)\\,⇏\\,(x=1)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, if $x=-3,$ then ${x}^{2}+2x-3=0,$ but $x\\ne 1.$\n\n- Condition $x<0$ is *not* a necessary condition:\n\n$$\n({x}^{2}+2x-3=0)\\,⇏\\,(x<0)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, if $x=1,$ then ${x}^{2}+2x-3=0,$ but $x≮0.$\n\n- Condition $|x|<5$ is a necessary condition:\n\n$$\n({x}^{2}+2x-3=0)\\,⇒\\,(|x|<5)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nEach solution of ${x}^{2}+2x-3=0$ satisfies $|x|<5.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $|x|<5$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152455 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152078 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ed7345a2-810f-5a35-aa01-092e40df06f3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sufficient Conditions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91a67b3a-5073-54f5-83fb-1d4270c77ded" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459635} {:answer/id #uuid "00f1eb19-3a97-5e5e-bc4a-3d6f902f3b3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459636}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "00f1eb19-3a97-5e5e-bc4a-3d6f902f3b3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459636} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ed263a7-bdad-5fde-b2c1-a3b2c00e98d7" :answer-field/key "$n=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460684} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ebd3a3c9-78a8-5b45-a7c2-e12e1f7c6ebc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459637} {:answer/id #uuid "e69723d1-75cb-53da-bce1-790336143d31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459638}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ebd3a3c9-78a8-5b45-a7c2-e12e1f7c6ebc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459637} :answer-field/id #uuid "dabd76d0-f9b1-5396-8d3e-7611c4cd25a2" :answer-field/key "$n<0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460685} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "393de18f-a9ee-572b-bea2-0808a050367a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459639} {:answer/id #uuid "202bc9f8-4641-55e1-a52d-fb0650489269" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459640}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "393de18f-a9ee-572b-bea2-0808a050367a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459639} :answer-field/id #uuid "43f5c05a-2aeb-5247-98c6-4a0b312f1cf7" :answer-field/key "$|n|<5$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460686}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b1189e0d-f1d2-59f2-9035-c87ca64ef4f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-172313" :question/problem "$\\,$ ${n}^{2}+2n-3=0$\n\nWhich of the following conditions are sufficient for the above to be true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ being true *guarantees* that $N$ must also be true. Therefore, $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- For $S$ to be true, it is *necessary* that $N$ is true. Therefore, $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$ However, note that $N$ being true does *not* guarantee that $S$ is true.\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nIn our case, we need to find the conditions that are *sufficient* for the given one:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,({n}^{2}+2n-3=0)\n$$\n\nNote that the solution to the given equation is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}^{2}+2n-3 & =0 \\\\ (n+3)(n-1) & =0 \\\\ n & =-3,1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given conditions.\n\n- Condition $n=1$ is a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(n=1)\\,⇒\\,({n}^{2}+2n-3=0)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nIf $n=1,$ then ${n}^{2}+2n-3=0.$\n\n- Condition $n<0$ is *not* a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(n<0)\\,⇏\\,({n}^{2}+2n-3=0)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, if $n=-1,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}^{2}+2n-3 & =(-1)^{2}+2(-1)-3 \\\\  & =1-2-3 \\\\  & =-4 \\\\  & \\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Condition $|n|<5$ is *not* a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(|n|<5)\\,⇏\\,({n}^{2}+2n-3=0)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, if $n=-1,$ then $|n|<5,$ but ${n}^{2}+2n-3\\ne 0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $n=1$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152500 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152066 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b70dd396-b01a-51e6-a52c-8ff729f48c45" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Standard Relation Is an Equivalence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bfdef795-e81e-55c2-9c40-b0592562b360" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459717} {:answer/id #uuid "28adba75-3ba2-5de1-bdd5-d2a1d6361b29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459718}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "28adba75-3ba2-5de1-bdd5-d2a1d6361b29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459718} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ce480b6-6617-54d9-ad65-d484f0eb7400" :answer-field/key "$R$ is reflexive" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460725} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b9fb294-83f5-513d-8c76-140d1249a9c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459719} {:answer/id #uuid "ca9f5620-0826-57cb-94c7-3bc826b5f4f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459720}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca9f5620-0826-57cb-94c7-3bc826b5f4f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459720} :answer-field/id #uuid "587c72ca-b75c-580c-9db4-bce4de9dedf5" :answer-field/key "$R$ is symmetric" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460726} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d2db4308-e16a-5148-81e9-6c4f6ba1ae2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459721} {:answer/id #uuid "ba6e62e4-faec-5caa-87b7-7466bb668966" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459722}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ba6e62e4-faec-5caa-87b7-7466bb668966" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459722} :answer-field/id #uuid "85ef0dd2-5351-57a9-b874-e14ffede21c7" :answer-field/key "$R$ is transitive" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460727} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d29be98-2715-5cb8-9c47-f3d0747dc8c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459723} {:answer/id #uuid "73b59ac6-4ce5-594a-92f2-9189d2014d47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459724}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73b59ac6-4ce5-594a-92f2-9189d2014d47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459724} :answer-field/id #uuid "5210d7f9-8d8a-5c74-b113-64a5686f2ca5" :answer-field/key "$R$ is an equivalence relation" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460728}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a2a24748-f2b1-5dae-9e25-ddb47fe6a36a" :question/math-academy-id "q-214134" :question/problem "Consider the following relation defined on the set $A$ containing all possible triangles in ${R}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nx\\,R\\,y\\,⇔\\,x≅y\n$$\n\nRecall that $x≅y$ means that $x$ and $y$ are congruent.\n\nWhich of the following are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given a relation $R$ on a set $A$:\n\n- $R$ is reflexive if and only if for all $x\\in A,$ $x\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is symmetric if and only if for all $x,y\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y,$ then $y\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is transitive if and only if for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y$ and $y\\,R\\,z,$ then $x\\,R\\,z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nLet's consider each of the properties in turn.\n\n- The relation $R$ is reflexive. For all $x\\in A,$ we have $x≅x.$ Every triangle is congruent with itself.\n\n- The relation $R$ is symmetric. For all $x,y\\in A,$ if $x≅y,$ then $y≅x.$ To see why, note that if we can find a sequence of rigid motions in the plane that maps $x$ to $y$ (implying $x≅y),$ then we can always find a sequence of rigid motions that maps $y$ to $x.$\n\n- The relation $R$ is transitive. For all $x,y,z\\in A,$ if $x≅y,$ and $y≅z,$ then $x≅z.$ To see why, note that if we can find a sequence of rigid motions in the plane that maps $x$ to $y$ (implying $x≅y)$ and another sequence that maps $y$ to $z,$ then we can always find a sequence that maps $x$ to $z.$\n\n- The relation $R$ is an equivalence relation since it's reflexive, symmetric, and transitive.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$R$ is reflexive”; “$R$ is symmetric”; “$R$ is transitive”; “$R$ is an equivalence relation”."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152502 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152067 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "968df6ec-e87e-5770-9c11-e7c8d8a27e6c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equivalence Relations on Finite Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81ab6736-6532-5393-8f42-1e394200da81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448484} {:answer/id #uuid "ebd59140-bce6-57a5-9a42-2dcf7ebc9a6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448485}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81ab6736-6532-5393-8f42-1e394200da81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448484} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0bb84ef-f6d5-57cf-ab00-d9e6c560633e" :answer-field/key "$R$ is reflexive" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449282} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae8e6f01-5d13-5abf-a602-4bf8348fc8bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448486} {:answer/id #uuid "472ea153-134a-55df-b4d5-6b90fcbcdc44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448487}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "472ea153-134a-55df-b4d5-6b90fcbcdc44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448487} :answer-field/id #uuid "643211dc-9039-55ef-9e7b-bb07e515c81c" :answer-field/key "$R$ is symmetric" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449283} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e56c714-9eae-5d92-ae7a-fc891040bb0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448488} {:answer/id #uuid "2b46950c-bc34-5268-a940-e31ed9180e60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448489}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e56c714-9eae-5d92-ae7a-fc891040bb0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448488} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c089e73-ed91-5a8b-9ca4-83eb63eaf923" :answer-field/key "$R$ is transitive" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449284} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cacd9eab-090e-5afe-8c09-b195213ed272" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448490} {:answer/id #uuid "af17e22c-cc51-54d8-bbd0-ce661facaf42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448491}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cacd9eab-090e-5afe-8c09-b195213ed272" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448490} :answer-field/id #uuid "3eb3fcfd-67ab-5b82-8f85-81448f13dc98" :answer-field/key "$R$ is an equivalence relation" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449285}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "14a51040-e179-5b66-9e0b-fca0e478f23c" :question/math-academy-id "q-214171" :question/problem "Consider the relation $R$ on the set $A={0,1,2}$ defined as \n\n$$\nR={(1,1),(0,2),(2,0)}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given a relation $R$ on a set $A$:\n\n- $R$ is reflexive if and only if for all $x\\in A,$ $x\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is symmetric if and only if for all $x,y\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y,$ then $y\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is transitive if and only if for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y$ and $y\\,R\\,z,$ then $x\\,R\\,z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nLet's consider each of the properties in turn.\n\n- The relation $R$ is *not* reflexive because  $(0,0)\\notin R.$\n\n- The relation $R$ is symmetric because $(y,x)\\in R$ whenever $(x,y)\\in R.$ $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- The relation $R$ is *not* transitive because $(0,2)\\in R$ and $(2,0)\\in R,$ but $(0,0)\\notin R$\n\n- The relation is *not* an equivalence relation since it's neither reflexive nor transitive.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$R$ is symmetric” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152569 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152280 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e66005fe-df33-590a-9d9c-91947cd4a608" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Fundamental Sets of Solutions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01457e13-545a-541f-acce-7e047fbcc408" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459799} {:answer/id #uuid "87fffe77-2143-5ff9-a2da-d1695227d7bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459800}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87fffe77-2143-5ff9-a2da-d1695227d7bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459800} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e5a869e-488e-5c2d-b679-699f90c7fb17" :answer-field/key "${y}_{1}(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)$ is a solution to the equation." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460766} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c86362a-34b4-52d6-ad75-a83bcdd09134" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459801} {:answer/id #uuid "f98b348b-31e2-5430-8135-c980ff086ccb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459802}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f98b348b-31e2-5430-8135-c980ff086ccb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459802} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd47a839-63c4-5a6d-b3f2-177b46628555" :answer-field/key "${y}_{2}(x)=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)$ is a solution to the equation." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460767} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d15df765-6a00-5bd1-8191-5dfbfb9a0320" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459803} {:answer/id #uuid "41ca8881-af27-5681-851a-1d131d4cd84d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459804}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d15df765-6a00-5bd1-8191-5dfbfb9a0320" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459803} :answer-field/id #uuid "2930a8aa-b164-5efa-ac05-ac74a56ddd9f" :answer-field/key "The functions ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ form a set of fundamental solutions to the equation." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460768}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f5244118-e12b-5ac2-ae1e-3e2ab9060947" :question/math-academy-id "q-333520" :question/problem "$$\n{y}^{″}+y=0\n$$\n\nConsider the differential equation above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that to determine whether $y(x)$ is a solution to the differential equation, we substitute $y$ and its derivatives into the equation. \n\nLet's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “${y}_{1}(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)$ is a solution to the equation” is true. First, we find the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{1}(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}^{′}(x) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) \\\\ {y}_{1}^{″}(x) & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's substitute ${y}_{1}(x)$ and its derivatives into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x) & =0 \\\\ 0 & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{1}(x)$ is a solution to the equation.\n\n- Statement “${y}_{2}(x)=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)$ is a solution to the equation” is true. First, we find the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{2}(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2}^{′}(x) & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) \\\\ {y}_{2}^{″}(x) & =-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's substitute ${y}_{2}(x)$ and its derivatives into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x) & =0 \\\\ 0 & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{2}(x)$ is a solution to the equation.\n\n- Statement “The functions ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ form a set of fundamental solutions to the equation” is false. Both ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are solutions of the equation. To check if these functions are linearly independent, we compute the Wronskian:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W({y}_{1},{y}_{2}) & =|\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}^{′} & {y}_{2}^{′}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x) & 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) & 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\cdot 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the  Wronskian equals $0$ for all $x\\in R,$ the functions are not linearly independent. Hence, ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ don't form a set of fundamental solutions to the equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${y}_{1}(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)$ is a solution to the equation”; “${y}_{2}(x)=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)$ is a solution to the equation” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152570 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152280 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e66005fe-df33-590a-9d9c-91947cd4a608" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Fundamental Sets of Solutions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d1e82711-ac51-5228-a804-1fa990c75224" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459805} {:answer/id #uuid "863f65d1-6c09-5fc7-9229-f2192ef8b701" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459806}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "863f65d1-6c09-5fc7-9229-f2192ef8b701" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459806} :answer-field/id #uuid "782a33f2-c589-5a92-89c3-730260ecc10a" :answer-field/key "${y}_{1}(x)={e}^{-x}$ is a solution to the equation." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460769} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d25a391a-473d-59a2-a939-6f566cc09ec1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459807} {:answer/id #uuid "b2ed9d3b-064f-5134-a779-fd16eac2b208" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459808}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d25a391a-473d-59a2-a939-6f566cc09ec1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459807} :answer-field/id #uuid "48062bbd-ee12-5738-a47f-04a9032c16f2" :answer-field/key "${y}_{2}(x)=1+{e}^{-x}$ is a solution to the equation." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460770} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a6bdefd-4eb4-5101-b957-85e5319b7fa8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459809} {:answer/id #uuid "92b100bd-b5bc-5ebe-a3ef-e3746c7a2aa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459810}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a6bdefd-4eb4-5101-b957-85e5319b7fa8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459809} :answer-field/id #uuid "f03c3346-2011-57c2-9e66-8f81c201e4aa" :answer-field/key "The functions ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ form a set of fundamental solutions to the equation." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460771}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7e7ec306-a94e-573b-92ac-0141248c8937" :question/math-academy-id "q-333522" :question/problem "$$\n{y}^{″}+7{y}^{′}+6y=0\n$$\n\nConsider the differential equation above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that to determine whether $y(x)$ is a solution to the differential equation, we substitute $y$ and its derivatives into the equation. \n\nLet's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “${y}_{1}(x)={e}^{-x}$ is a solution to the equation” is true. We find the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{1}(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}^{′}(x) & =-{e}^{-x} \\\\ {y}_{1}^{″}(x) & ={e}^{-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's substitute ${y}_{1}(x)$ and its derivatives into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-x}+7(-{e}^{-x})+6{e}^{-x} & =0 \\\\ 0 & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{1}(x)$ is a solution to the equation.\n\n- Statement “${y}_{2}(x)=1+{e}^{-x}$ is a solution to the equation” is false. We find the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{2}(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2}^{′}(x) & =-{e}^{-x} \\\\ {y}_{2}^{″}(x) & ={e}^{-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's substitute ${y}_{2}(x)$ and its derivatives into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-x}+7(-{e}^{-x})+6(1+{e}^{-x}) & =0 \\\\ 6 & =0\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{2}(x)$ is not a solution to the equation.\n\n- Statement “The functions ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ form a set of fundamental solutions to the equation” is false. Since ${y}_{2}(x)$ is not a solution of the given differential equation, ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ don't form a set of fundamental solutions to the equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${y}_{1}(x)={e}^{-x}$ is a solution to the equation” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152586 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152220 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aee17e3a-031d-5c0e-9488-17410b3a2372" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Dimensions of Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d08482b-821f-56f3-8c0f-211f5fff39f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477259} {:answer/id #uuid "6802104b-0013-5421-9de4-04f55fc881af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477260}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6802104b-0013-5421-9de4-04f55fc881af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477260} :answer-field/id #uuid "b235e173-6128-58d6-9a96-0def6a5ebeb8" :answer-field/key "${R}_{5}[t]$, the vector space of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $5$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477599} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c730b7cc-bbcf-54da-bc02-31569666a929" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477261} {:answer/id #uuid "c555688b-8252-5103-ba27-0ec6e204163b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477262}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c730b7cc-bbcf-54da-bc02-31569666a929" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477261} :answer-field/id #uuid "a958704a-837e-541b-a3d8-6ad826d0ce4e" :answer-field/key "${R}^{5}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477600} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "927c0d03-b501-5ac0-b7a7-133f0fc51e65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477263} {:answer/id #uuid "61cefcd5-f8ef-5942-b4c9-557bbdda8878" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477264}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "927c0d03-b501-5ac0-b7a7-133f0fc51e65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477263} :answer-field/id #uuid "73c3fb05-5c30-5ebb-a2d1-6b394d24d8c9" :answer-field/key "${\\text{M}}_{6}(R),$ the vector space of all $6\\times 6$ matrices over $R$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477601}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c3e2a498-b435-555d-acbe-67f3af373b5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-36477" :question/problem "Which of the following vector spaces has a dimension of $6?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the vector spaces in turn.\n\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}_{n}[t])=n+1.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}_{5}[t])=5+1=6.\\,✓\n$$\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}^{n})=n.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}^{5})=5\\ne 6.\\,\\times \n$$\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{n}(R))={n}^{2}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{6}(R))={6}^{2}=36\\ne 6.\\,\\times \n$$\n\nHence, the correct answer is “${R}_{5}[t]$, the vector space of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $5$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152632 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152276 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d0a7ede-b896-56c6-9b60-a6aec8eff9e8" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Second-Order Initial Value Problems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e77d06e-75de-5efc-a31a-08ab5cd28827" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460125} {:answer/id #uuid "d7273db4-f030-554b-9eb4-1f8ad7088e10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460126}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7273db4-f030-554b-9eb4-1f8ad7088e10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460126} :answer-field/id #uuid "7255451a-6f73-5904-b058-7ec744515ab6" :answer-field/key "$x{y}^{″}-2{y}^{′}+y$ $={x}^{2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ $\\,y(1)$ $=0,$ $\\,{y}^{′}(1)$ $=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460929} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e1476747-7cd7-5321-b84b-6e1235b6e7e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460127} {:answer/id #uuid "f91c9644-913e-582a-adaf-b144e1e7ea1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460128}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e1476747-7cd7-5321-b84b-6e1235b6e7e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460127} :answer-field/id #uuid "e14339dc-b2b5-545f-aa5f-519565543cd4" :answer-field/key "${x}^{2}{y}^{″}-x{y}^{′}+y=10$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460930} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3da02e26-cd27-5a84-95fc-65e7c16865c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460129} {:answer/id #uuid "c0f92fd3-cff0-5229-b161-7053c1989dfb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460130}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3da02e26-cd27-5a84-95fc-65e7c16865c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460129} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf992f83-6c65-58e9-a6aa-5bc334f98c34" :answer-field/key "${x}^{2}{y}^{″}-4x{y}^{′}+16y$ $=0,$ $\\,y(0)$ $=0,$ $\\,{y}^{′}(2)$ $=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460931}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2c0602e3-c50d-5991-b1fc-f704c082ddef" :question/math-academy-id "q-65014" :question/problem "Which of the following systems is an initial value problem?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "If a second-order differential equation for the function $y(x)$ is given with two conditions specified at the *same* location in the domain of $y,$ then this is an **initial value problem**.\n\nLet's go through each equation in turn.\n\n- The first system is an initial value problem. The differential equation is together with two conditions at the same location in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=1$).\n\n- The second system is not an initial value problem. It contains an equation only. No conditions are specified.\n\n- The third system is not an initial value problem. It consists of a differential equation together with two conditions at different points in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=0$ and $x=2$). This is a **boundary value problem.**"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152634 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152192 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "42bc95a3-4e0c-5487-8427-31cee0ecf80b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Solutions of Linear ODEs Using the Sum Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75241296-7d49-5ca1-956a-c38b114182cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460131} {:answer/id #uuid "fd89f6a8-704b-542d-b4cf-4a6f6fe0111a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460132}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd89f6a8-704b-542d-b4cf-4a6f6fe0111a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460132} :answer-field/id #uuid "6099e4a8-ed0b-5342-8225-9b646ac9e526" :answer-field/key "$y(x)={e}^{x}+{e}^{2x}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460932} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d9816c67-e577-5ad4-b7f8-b456b0361276" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460133} {:answer/id #uuid "27592d46-4cea-5d31-b285-b1e4f988dacd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460134}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9816c67-e577-5ad4-b7f8-b456b0361276" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460133} :answer-field/id #uuid "54550bb8-14b1-57b6-b59e-e95e4bbdf6c2" :answer-field/key "$y(x)={e}^{x}\\cdot {e}^{2x}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460933} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "894e7a98-0c2b-5873-8c77-7c3eb7d45b3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460135} {:answer/id #uuid "ca7bffe3-1408-59e7-ba58-734114cb573e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460136}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "894e7a98-0c2b-5873-8c77-7c3eb7d45b3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460135} :answer-field/id #uuid "44abc534-51c3-532d-b919-1296780151a3" :answer-field/key "$y(x)=\\frac{{e}^{x}}{{e}^{2x}}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460934}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "03be4c64-335b-58c9-94d2-aea65ff76ae9" :question/math-academy-id "q-65077" :question/problem "Given that ${y}_{1}(x)={e}^{x}$ and ${y}_{2}(x)={e}^{2x}$ are solutions to the equation ${y}^{″}-3{y}^{′}+2y=0,$ then according to the superposition principle which of the following must also be a solution to the equation?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "According to the superposition principle, if the functions ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ are solutions to a homogeneous, linear differential equation, then $y(x)={y}_{1}(x)+{y}_{2}(x)$ is also a solution to the equation.\n\nLet's consider each option:\n\n- The function $y(x)={e}^{x}+{e}^{2x}$ is a solution of the equation by the superposition principle.\n\n- The function $y(x)={e}^{x}\\cdot {e}^{2x}$ is **not** guaranteed to be a solution of the equation by the superposition principle. The superposition principle does not extend to the products of the known solutions.\n\n- The function $y(x)=\\frac{{e}^{x}}{{e}^{2x}}$ is **not** guaranteed to be a solution of the equation by the superposition principle. The superposition principle does not extend to the quotients of the known solutions.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $y(x)={e}^{x}+{e}^{2x}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152731 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152263 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bfbebc20-1b48-5718-a057-b743c8af8de1" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bijections For Functions Defined on the Set of Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3677e56c-6799-57b0-a2d4-f62b70624054" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477413} {:answer/id #uuid "986ca73f-18b3-50fc-93d5-8e624b067635" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477414}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3677e56c-6799-57b0-a2d4-f62b70624054" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477413} :answer-field/id #uuid "e79b7a06-269e-5a7e-94eb-e32048cbf57a" :answer-field/key "The function is an injection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477676} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d7494d5-369a-50ec-84c5-6ae29165167e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477415} {:answer/id #uuid "432bc379-c608-5673-b288-439236462e6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477416}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d7494d5-369a-50ec-84c5-6ae29165167e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477415} :answer-field/id #uuid "21693608-ac7d-5fa0-ad21-5b2b41f2c025" :answer-field/key "The function is a surjection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477677} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7b823b5-896c-5e38-9546-157a5a41bc8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477417} {:answer/id #uuid "19fe52d7-263e-54d5-b802-087079d99e8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477418}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7b823b5-896c-5e38-9546-157a5a41bc8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477417} :answer-field/id #uuid "acae7c55-2445-5861-bd53-dba6dee4e0e4" :answer-field/key "The function is a bijection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477678}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ed18a3e4-6415-576f-b0e6-2282d7b910ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-76219" :question/problem "For the function $f:R\\to R$ defined by $f(x)={x}^{2},$ which of the following  statements are true? \n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a function $f:X\\to Y$ is \n\n- an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ whenever $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2},$\n\n- a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y,$\n\n- a bijection if it is both a surjection and an injection.\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement “The function is an injection” is false. For instance, $f(2)=4=f(-2)$, but $2\\ne -2.$ So, $f(x)$ is not an injection.\n\n- Statement “The function is a surjection” is false. For example, there is no $x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=-1.$ So, $f(x)$ is not a surjection.\n\n- Statement “The function is a bijection” is false because the function is not both an injection and a surjection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152732 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152135 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6fa67074-d3c8-5000-95a3-7f935936ab7d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Surjections For Functions Defined Algebraically"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ce23f03c-32be-576f-b060-ea74e6f090fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477419} {:answer/id #uuid "95c018bb-a80b-54fc-af45-bef9a800aa6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477420}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95c018bb-a80b-54fc-af45-bef9a800aa6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477420} :answer-field/id #uuid "807cf1ab-8d42-5a68-ba3b-58e1293a4d47" :answer-field/key "$f:R\\to (0,\\infty )$ defined by $f(x)={3}^{x}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477679} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c73e61da-f236-522d-a83f-180053be0d94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477421} {:answer/id #uuid "73bef137-63b7-5b4d-885b-e636dd0af2c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477422}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c73e61da-f236-522d-a83f-180053be0d94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477421} :answer-field/id #uuid "da627b86-eb71-5917-ad11-3aa68e6d2771" :answer-field/key "$g:Q\\to Q$ defined by $g(x)={x}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477680} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85c9ed27-d7c8-5ae2-aba1-099c3f60cf33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477423} {:answer/id #uuid "acdf2aa1-86d9-5db4-b85c-1752a695bf14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477424}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "85c9ed27-d7c8-5ae2-aba1-099c3f60cf33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477423} :answer-field/id #uuid "8bc7e146-01f9-59d3-8a9a-3934e62a5feb" :answer-field/key "$h:R\\to R$ defined by $h(x)={x}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477681}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e0a2fe09-79e7-541d-8328-5d8abf9635ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-76236" :question/problem "Which of the following functions are surjections?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A function $f:X\\to Y$ is a **surjection** (also known as **onto**) if, for *every* element $y$ in $Y,$ there is at least one element in $X$ that maps to $y.$ \n\nSymbolically, we can write:\n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each function.\n\n- “$f:R\\to (0,\\infty )$ defined by $f(x)={3}^{x}$” is a surjection. Given $y\\in (0,\\infty ),$ choose $x={log}_{3}⁡y\\in R.$ Then $f(x)=f({log}_{3}⁡y)={3}^{{log}_{3}⁡y}=y.$\n\n- “$g:Q\\to Q$ defined by $g(x)={x}^{2}$” is *not* a surjection. As a counterexample, choose $2\\in Q.$ There is no number $x\\in Q$ such that $g(x)=2.$ The only real solutions of $g(x)={x}^{2}=2$ are $x=\\pm\\sqrt{2}$, and neither belongs to $Q$.\n\n- “$h:R\\to R$ defined by $h(x)={x}^{2}$” is *not* a surjection. As a counterexample, choose $-1\\in R.$ There is no number $x\\in R$ such that $h(x)={x}^{2}=-1.$  In fact, ${x}^{2}\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in R$, with equality at $x=0$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$f:R\\to (0,\\infty )$ defined by $f(x)={3}^{x}$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152736 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152265 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f237343d-2f8a-5a9f-9e5f-c9f22784547a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bijections For Functions Functions Defined Algebraically"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "685ac942-8b8e-5612-a051-b4401b2b86f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477425} {:answer/id #uuid "d45fba76-4b8a-55c3-b76b-46d97a1971aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477426}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "685ac942-8b8e-5612-a051-b4401b2b86f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477425} :answer-field/id #uuid "de3496e2-fb30-52e3-8c03-68e6aa524658" :answer-field/key "$f:R\\to R$ defined by $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477682} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0951c26f-04d3-5a60-9632-f376e2b06817" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477427} {:answer/id #uuid "96421230-be9f-5dfb-9225-a1c449a6cb42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477428}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0951c26f-04d3-5a60-9632-f376e2b06817" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477427} :answer-field/id #uuid "95cda1d1-a0f1-5091-acb2-e5f07ffc5b16" :answer-field/key "$g:Q\\to Q$ defined by $g(x)={x}^{2}-2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477683} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bd240d9-24ff-5735-b1d1-6ae3d7e5603f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477429} {:answer/id #uuid "4b0030ea-cc6c-5c40-ae03-08ed65178645" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477430}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b0030ea-cc6c-5c40-ae03-08ed65178645" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477430} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b838ec4-e617-53b2-8781-b7f56025c343" :answer-field/key "$h:Q\\to Q$ defined by $h(x)=8x-3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477684}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6f83b131-cba7-5925-800d-f4bed8f0ae07" :question/math-academy-id "q-76250" :question/problem "Which of the following functions are bijections?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a function $f:X\\to Y$ is a bijection if it is both a surjection and an injection.\n\n- “$f:R\\to R$ defined by $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$” is *not* a bijection because it is not surjective. Remember that the range of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ is $[-1,1].$ This means that \n\n$$\n-1\\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\le 1.\n$$\n\nSo,  for example, there is no value $x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=2.$\n\n- “$g:Q\\to Q$ defined by $g(x)={x}^{2}-2$” is *not* a bijection because it is not injective. For example, $1$ and $-1$ are distinct elements of $Q$, but $g(1)=-1=g(-1)$.\n\n- “$h:Q\\to Q$ defined by $h(x)=8x-3$” is a bijection. First of all, it is a surjection because $∀\\,y\\in Q,$ we can choose an $x\\in Q$ such that $h(x)=y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h(x) & =y \\\\ 8x-3 & =y \\\\ x & =\\frac{y+3}{8}\\in Q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe verify that, \n\n$$\nh(x)=h\\left(\\frac{y+3}{8}\\right)=8\\left(\\frac{y+3}{8}\\right)-3=y.\n$$\n\nSecond, it is an injection: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h({x}_{1}) & =h({x}_{2}) \\\\ 8{x}_{1}-3 & =8{x}_{2}-3 \\\\ {x}_{1} & ={x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause $h$ is both surjective and injective, $h$ is bijective.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$h:Q\\to Q$ defined by $h(x)=8x-3$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152737 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152264 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f12e21e5-0a96-5f87-9642-d63d23e0038a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bijections For Functions Whose Domains or Codomains Are Real Intervals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16d64db2-6826-5251-8ae3-7fe008999428" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477431} {:answer/id #uuid "6b9b36a1-1bcc-5f12-b931-8f36d644dbc3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477432}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "16d64db2-6826-5251-8ae3-7fe008999428" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477431} :answer-field/id #uuid "425a8449-3679-511b-86e3-08edefce31fe" :answer-field/key "The function is an injection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477685} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "97c1af68-eb7a-5fb4-9d23-51ac1a9cde47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477433} {:answer/id #uuid "9f03229b-6e06-53b3-a58c-01f718fe6e7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477434}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f03229b-6e06-53b3-a58c-01f718fe6e7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477434} :answer-field/id #uuid "3fa1678d-f52a-58be-85d3-499bde13d65b" :answer-field/key "The function is a surjection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477686} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ce56477d-c793-5650-b9c5-93714ec8795a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477435} {:answer/id #uuid "707a10c2-1ed7-52dd-b7b0-bad8a477f27a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477436}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce56477d-c793-5650-b9c5-93714ec8795a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477435} :answer-field/id #uuid "033d9b08-7cbe-56d2-9cf3-19b39701cc1f" :answer-field/key "The function is a bijection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477687}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "16a1e15e-b250-589e-b4bc-6048810dc9dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-76259" :question/problem "![](images/06/06e3c48955dc8f907c87a93aeaa7c2a7240ea194fe1ca6a96b2a0bf566882264.png)\n\nFor the function $f:R\\to [0,\\infty )$ defined by $f(x)=0.25{x}^{2}$, which of the following statements are true? \n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a function $f:X\\to Y$ is \n\n- an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ whenever $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2},$\n\n- a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y,$\n\n- a bijection if it is both a surjection and an injection.\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement “The function is an injection” is false. There are horizontal lines (like the one depicted below) that cross the graph of $f(x)$ more than once. So, $∃\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R$ such that ${x}_{1}\\ne {x}_{2}$ but $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}).$\n\n![](images/fc/fce55ada0375bff9bd3ea5852e80f707d70f145211b60e80b5a16b3049020000.png)\n\n          \n\n- Statement “The function is a surjection” is true. According to the graph, the range of $f(x)$ indeed covers the interval $[0,\\infty ).$\n\n- Statement “The function is a bijection” is false because the function is not an injection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The function is a surjection” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152747 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152074 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2eebe007-8a95-578d-b553-e37a7bd8a327" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Congruent Negative Integers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f978570c-6580-56e1-9460-5f3214d1f235" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448750} {:answer/id #uuid "ed6dce31-f022-5946-8902-518a0e2bbb17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448751}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed6dce31-f022-5946-8902-518a0e2bbb17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448751} :answer-field/id #uuid "8410ec4c-458f-57e2-a7b5-f09e80fe4fd2" :answer-field/key "$11≡1\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449415} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60ab0c5e-37fd-575e-88ad-4464abb84a76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448752} {:answer/id #uuid "b8688616-ef55-51cb-bbfa-70d3e1a518c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448753}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60ab0c5e-37fd-575e-88ad-4464abb84a76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448752} :answer-field/id #uuid "01241a79-73a4-5696-b5e9-6c65ff7c2ea0" :answer-field/key "$27≡15\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449416} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f133b002-888e-5134-8f6c-ef0184bf7602" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448754} {:answer/id #uuid "7a09dde9-800a-50d3-9937-ae0eff18239d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448755}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a09dde9-800a-50d3-9937-ae0eff18239d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448755} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b47060f-60ac-5389-8d01-2fc48cd65978" :answer-field/key "$30≡-18\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449417}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bc725849-ec72-5565-a2a3-c18e7bade536" :question/math-academy-id "q-76784" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we recall that \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,n∣(a-b).\n$$\n\nSo, $a$ and $b$ are congruent modulo $n$ if and only if $(a-b)$ is divisible by $n$ (there is no remainder).\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $11≡1\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5)$ is true because $5∣(11-1).$ There is no remainder:\n\n$$\n(11-1)÷5=10÷5=2\n$$\n\n- Statement $27≡15\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)$ is false because $7∤(27-15).$ Notice that $27-15=12,$ which is not divisible by $7.$\n\n- Statement $30≡-18\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4)$ is true because $4\\,|\\,(30-(-18)).$ There is no remainder:\n\n$$\n(30-(-18))÷4=48÷4=12\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $11≡1\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5)$; $30≡-18\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4)$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152754 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152257 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dacfbca6-6135-5d51-a07e-627fce79dfd1" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equivalence Classes Containing a Given Element"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b8a3121-c55a-53c7-b85d-0d7cc04d7d29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460197} {:answer/id #uuid "00b6d4c4-56c3-5ee1-8ac1-829a4efc942a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460198}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "00b6d4c4-56c3-5ee1-8ac1-829a4efc942a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460198} :answer-field/id #uuid "4cb9bbb4-a63c-5a79-bf32-93b2e53d24ec" :answer-field/key "$[-1]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460965} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eac28bb6-8d8b-59a9-b7e9-41f288d9ed10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460199} {:answer/id #uuid "3e351bb2-929c-546f-96f1-8200b0d06341" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460200}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e351bb2-929c-546f-96f1-8200b0d06341" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460200} :answer-field/id #uuid "0fe8ced8-6627-5358-839d-26c7a572c952" :answer-field/key "$[-i]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460966} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ec7797a-5231-5617-bda8-babbfffb3f71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460201} {:answer/id #uuid "7d0b73dc-aba2-5005-a4d2-809c22405838" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460202}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ec7797a-5231-5617-bda8-babbfffb3f71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460201} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8c3a302-4930-5c70-a406-af398dd21cf8" :answer-field/key "$[2i]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460967}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "57bb64c1-83a8-5ad6-a9bc-3ab2aa9fabbd" :question/math-academy-id "q-76893" :question/problem "Consider the equivalence relation $∼$ on $C,$ defined by $x∼y$ if ${x}^{4}={y}^{4}.$ Which of the following equivalence classes contain the element $i?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We have $i\\in [x]$ if $i∼x.$ Using the definition of the given equivalence relation, we require\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{i}^{4} & ={x}^{4} \\\\ 1 & ={x}^{4} \\\\ {x}^{4} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's now consider each of the given equivalence classes.\n\n- $i\\in [-1]$ because $(-1)^{4}=1\\,✓$\n\n- $i\\in [-i]$ because $(-i)^{4}=1\\,✓$\n\n- $i\\notin [2i]$ because $(2i)^{4}=16\\ne 1\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $[-1]$; $[-i]$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152758 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152073 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "398716c2-d0e6-5106-a702-2f71d957726f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Congruent Integers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1790ea95-c04e-5e74-9ebe-478d69ec14ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448756} {:answer/id #uuid "9cffea29-ce10-5b82-b6f0-fda0b3748bf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448757}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1790ea95-c04e-5e74-9ebe-478d69ec14ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448756} :answer-field/id #uuid "b03b37de-484b-5600-a01c-691628ffc5ae" :answer-field/key "$19≡5\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449418} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "920a8ce9-af55-5bb8-a0b2-55fb72f836be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448758} {:answer/id #uuid "c0ada1f3-d53f-5796-82b5-46b26051243e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448759}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0ada1f3-d53f-5796-82b5-46b26051243e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448759} :answer-field/id #uuid "4cd4257f-7d31-5e46-acef-fbfc5fe8607e" :answer-field/key "$22≡7\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449419} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4118f2bf-38f3-5c06-9e58-43a705ca04e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448760} {:answer/id #uuid "5200f51c-731d-5dcf-aa54-116cb1aefd56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448761}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4118f2bf-38f3-5c06-9e58-43a705ca04e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448760} :answer-field/id #uuid "75c31522-73f1-59dd-b623-71de9752ce3c" :answer-field/key "$20≡9\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449420}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "665aa776-ec33-596f-ae58-1e8a076473e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-76952" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we recall that \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,n∣(a-b).\n$$\n\nSo, $a$ and $b$ are congruent modulo $n$ if and only if $(a-b)$ is divisible by $n$ (there is no remainder).\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $19≡5\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4)$ is false because $4∤(19-5).$ Notice that $19-5=14,$ which is not divisible by $4.$\n\n- Statement $22≡7\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)$ is true because $3∣(22-7).$ There is no remainder:\n\n$$\n(22-7)÷3=15÷3=5\n$$\n\n- Statement $20≡9\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)$ is false because $8∤(20-9).$ Notice that $20-5=15,$ which is not divisible by $4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $22≡7\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152767 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152135 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6fa67074-d3c8-5000-95a3-7f935936ab7d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Surjections For Functions Defined Algebraically"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7601f872-b952-5d20-9302-47c936e401df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477437} {:answer/id #uuid "6b852444-ff85-5d44-a23f-38a5914d53df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477438}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7601f872-b952-5d20-9302-47c936e401df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477437} :answer-field/id #uuid "82fa40a5-9b33-5114-84f0-0a4f27810a63" :answer-field/key "$f:{0,1,2}\\to {1,3,9,27}$ defined by $f(x)={3}^{x}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477688} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e04e4c3c-d3f7-5aba-9278-b6ecf053db53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477439} {:answer/id #uuid "02f8d3cc-ba76-5a75-875a-593239657546" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477440}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e04e4c3c-d3f7-5aba-9278-b6ecf053db53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477439} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d109356-ec15-5dd2-a512-bc0df803865b" :answer-field/key "$g:[0,\\infty )\\to R$ defined by $g(x)={x}^{3}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477689} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d335b7f-35c5-575a-9100-ef3ce38e5197" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477441} {:answer/id #uuid "bac7840c-d9c1-5b20-bc77-57fd938ed351" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477442}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bac7840c-d9c1-5b20-bc77-57fd938ed351" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477442} :answer-field/id #uuid "4fcf8bdb-b3c8-53d9-8c44-24cf872e39aa" :answer-field/key "$h:{0,1,2}\\to {-1,1,3}$ defined by $h(x)=2x-1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477690}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b4cd6be0-845e-5684-aa03-e5a2472b9ab4" :question/math-academy-id "q-77378" :question/problem "Which of the following functions are surjections?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A function $f:X\\to Y$ is a **surjection** (also known as **onto**) if, for *every* element $y$ in $Y,$ there is at least one element in $X$ that maps to $y.$ \n\nSymbolically, we can write:\n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each function.\n\n- “$f:{0,1,2}\\to {1,3,9,27}$ defined by $f(x)={3}^{x}$” is *not* a surjection. As a counterexample, choose $27$ from the codomain. The only number $x$ that satisfies $f(x)={3}^{x}=27$ is $x=3,$ but $3\\notin {0,1,2}.$\n\n- “$g:[0,\\infty )\\to R$ defined by $g(x)={x}^{3}$” is *not* a surjection. As a counterexample, choose $-1\\in R.$ There is no number $x\\in [0,\\infty )$ such that $g(x)=-1.$ The only number $x$ that satisfies $g(x)={x}^{3}=-1$ is $x=-1,$ but $-1\\notin [0,\\infty ).$\n\n- “$h:{0,1,2}\\to {-1,1,3}$ defined by $h(x)=2x-1$” is a surjection. Indeed, $h(0)=-1,$ $h(1)=1$ and $h(2)=3.$ So, for every $y\\in {-1,1,3},$ there exists an element $x\\in {0,1,2}$ such that $h(x)=y.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$h:{0,1,2}\\to {-1,1,3}$ defined by $h(x)=2x-1$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152792 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152097 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d2f207a-8e99-5520-ab9f-266c8f54465b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Elements Belonging to a Residue Class"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e36ef6d-631b-52d5-8dcf-a3163bedefc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460209} {:answer/id #uuid "bd99744b-e643-5e94-8726-2bfacb366109" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460210}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd99744b-e643-5e94-8726-2bfacb366109" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460210} :answer-field/id #uuid "63b26e83-37cb-521c-b74d-33d58c0ea6f4" :answer-field/key "The number $-12$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460971} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69a8cf14-62a1-52b7-8e43-d8191005ec7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460211} {:answer/id #uuid "20be12cc-42f7-55a8-bdf1-917eebf1a93d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460212}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "69a8cf14-62a1-52b7-8e43-d8191005ec7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460211} :answer-field/id #uuid "71fd13b3-1e85-56d2-837c-5fa3662e3c8d" :answer-field/key "The number $3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460972} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "afc96503-5873-5b58-841f-5c0a4fed324d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460213} {:answer/id #uuid "1d61e050-7b0c-570a-8891-cdc5dab33f8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460214}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d61e050-7b0c-570a-8891-cdc5dab33f8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460214} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0cd9155-6655-58f5-95b3-349f13d7bad1" :answer-field/key "The number $24$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460973}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ba3bb1ff-f2f2-5531-a68f-b27801ed7066" :question/math-academy-id "q-78598" :question/problem "Which of the following integers belong to the residue class $[6]_{9}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The residue class $[6]_{9}$ consists of the elements that are congruent to $6$ modulo $9.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[6]_{9} & =\\{x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡6\\,(\\text{mod}\\,9)\\} \\\\  & =\\{x\\in Z\\,|\\,x=6+9k,\\,k\\in Z\\} \\\\  & =\\{6+9k\\,|\\,k\\in Z\\} \\\\  & =\\{…,\\,6-2\\cdot 9,\\,6-9,\\,6,\\,6+9,\\,6+2\\cdot 9,\\,…\\} \\\\  & =\\{…,-12,-3,6,15,24,…\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $-12$ and $24$ belong to $[6]_{9},$ while $3$ does not.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The number $-12$”; “The number $24$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152809 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152192 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "42bc95a3-4e0c-5487-8427-31cee0ecf80b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Solutions of Linear ODEs Using the Sum Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19ac0897-f919-5edf-bf78-26e13f92883d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460227} {:answer/id #uuid "5cac7a37-3782-5a73-b5ca-7a757aae2a8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460228}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19ac0897-f919-5edf-bf78-26e13f92883d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460227} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f68fb17-bbf0-5de2-a733-f061bc57f907" :answer-field/key "$y(x)=(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460980} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38299350-adac-58c2-b237-ae74f9e17918" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460229} {:answer/id #uuid "d576b556-948d-5f01-85dd-7dbbbbb23e10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460230}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38299350-adac-58c2-b237-ae74f9e17918" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460229} :answer-field/id #uuid "f893192f-f2df-574d-b0f9-690d9e384ab5" :answer-field/key "$y(x)=x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460981} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88d4d6b6-5445-510e-9981-988d2a0d34df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460231} {:answer/id #uuid "70814542-0d28-542a-97d6-915bb53990c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460232}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70814542-0d28-542a-97d6-915bb53990c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460232} :answer-field/id #uuid "d26bf839-1097-5aab-ab35-a98e10712050" :answer-field/key "$y(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460982}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "46b25723-729d-510e-b94e-77440edfe286" :question/math-academy-id "q-79724" :question/problem "Given that ${y}_{1}(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and ${y}_{2}(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ are solutions to a homogeneous, linear, second-order ODE, then according to the superposition principle which of the following must also be a solution to the equation?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "According to the superposition principle, if the functions ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ are solutions to a homogeneous, linear differential equation, then $y(x)={y}_{1}(x)+{y}_{2}(x)$ is also a solution to the equation.\n\nLet's consider each option:\n\n- The function $y(x)=(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{2}$ is **not** guaranteed to be a solution of the equation by the superposition principle. The superposition principle does not extend to the product of the known solutions.\n\n- The function $y(x)=x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ is **not** guaranteed to be a solution of the equation by the superposition principle. The superposition principle does not extend to the product of a function and the known solutions.\n\n- The function $y(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ is a solution of the equation by the superposition principle.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $y(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152811 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152193 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0829d4a-239a-5a8e-9c8e-3cdc76a993bc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Solutions of Linear ODEs Using the Constant Multiple Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87ddde79-2216-55f9-a241-4e3672b694c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460233} {:answer/id #uuid "0b7a88de-d9d2-5ec0-a2fb-a186b71ec20e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460234}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87ddde79-2216-55f9-a241-4e3672b694c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460233} :answer-field/id #uuid "e844d229-6b8b-51c9-b888-0ba89abf3b5b" :answer-field/key "$y(x)={sin}^{2}⁡(2x)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460983} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eeab3a09-b1a6-5339-9628-ec71bce3f490" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460235} {:answer/id #uuid "c845b3e9-cf61-58a4-9310-d63f07f4f147" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460236}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c845b3e9-cf61-58a4-9310-d63f07f4f147" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460236} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f15e339-1689-5c7f-8cf5-50895397afc6" :answer-field/key "$y(x)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460984} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7904cf0f-78cb-5a70-8792-6d23e6d0e9de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460237} {:answer/id #uuid "d97c94c7-45b3-50e5-a408-e6bc7d86f4ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460238}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7904cf0f-78cb-5a70-8792-6d23e6d0e9de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460237} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9b85a7e-07f0-5732-a416-1ae1d52c3ca4" :answer-field/key "$y(x)={x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460985}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f6e0c318-7db3-5a86-afe7-c1d5265937a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-79730" :question/problem "Given that ${y}_{1}(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)$ is a solution to a homogeneous, linear, second-order ODE, then according to the superposition principle which of the following must also be a solution to the equation?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "According to the superposition principle, if the function ${y}_{1}(x)$ is a solution to a homogeneous, linear differential equation, and $c$ is a constant, then $y(x)=c{y}_{1}(x)$ is also a solution to the equation.\n\nLet's consider each option:\n\n- The function $y(x)={sin}^{2}⁡(2x)$ is **not** guaranteed to be a solution of the equation by the superposition principle. The superposition principle does not extend to the product of known solutions.\n\n- The function $y(x)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)$ is a solution of the equation by the superposition principle. In this case, $c=-1.$\n\n- The function $y(x)={x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)$ is **not** guaranteed to be a solution of the equation by the superposition principle. The superposition principle does not extend to the product of a non-constant function and a known solution.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $y(x)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)$ only."}]
